This Effect is used by GraphicsDevice.Present to anti-alias the finished frame (FXAA),
when the player turns "fxaa" on in WPR's settings.

FxaaEffect.fxb is YUVToRGBAEffect.fxb with its pixel shader swapped for the one in
FxaaEffect.ps.asm (its vertex shader just passes position and texcoord through). It has no
parameters of its own: the size of one texel rides in the quad's vertices (texcoord zw, see
GraphicsDevice.WprFxaaVertex), because dsx/dsy need an extension on GLSL ES 1.00. make_fxb.py also
patches two things MojoShader's assembler cannot express: the ps_3_0 texcoord0 input's usage (it
writes 0, which links against POSITION0 and fails) and the vertex shader's texcoord write mask
(.xy -> .xyzw, so zw reach the pixel shader).

To rebuild after changing the assembly (MojoShader's assembler is in
Src/Backends/FNA.Platform/lib/FNA3D/MojoShader):
  1. assemble FxaaEffect.ps.asm to bytecode with MOJOSHADER_assemble
  2. python3 make_fxb.py ../YUVToRGBA/YUVToRGBAEffect.fxb ps.bin FxaaEffect.fxb
It was checked with MojoShader's own effect parser against the glsl, glsles and spirv profiles.
